From 10bb461d04a70f42d11b1e6573b68c6246919d40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:26:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] rails: fun_coins, fun_quote, fun_mine, fun_send and
 fun_launch

The coins of the site a node follows, as functions its model can call:
where each is on its two curves and what a coin costs on each, blocks to
mine on a coin's QWEN curve (the qwen they will owe moved in under the
node's spending rail), coins given away by the launch's own node, and a new
coin made through the site. Like graph_tip and draw they are not in the
template: the node's loop offers fun_mine and fun_launch in its turns
(talk.MIND_OFFERS_FUN), with one sentence of the site's own words, and a
coin's name reaches the model as data. tools/chain.py starts the helper
as fun, stops it with the others and shows its lines in status.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014XWxCQ3HRkxqr38zmdadwu
